Date: 2025-11-15

Summary of updates and fixes

Backend
- Python env: Standardized on Python 3.11 with venv; updated setup flow.
- Dependencies: Resolved Windows-native build issues; pinned numpy==1.26.4; removed conflicting langchain packages; added langchain-text-splitters.
- Chroma: Reset persisted DB to resolve schema mismatch; vector store stable.
- Ollama: Verified service and models; integrated robust connection handling.
- Streaming fix: Avoid closing shared httpx AsyncClient; fixed "client has been closed" error in WebSocket streaming.
- Static files: Mounted /files to serve uploaded PDFs; retained uploads for linking.
- Prompts: Enhanced SYSTEM_PROMPT to include a minimal JSON matches summary at the end of answers for UI parsing.

API/Services
- RAG pipeline: Streams tokens, exposes sources; records last retrieved sources for post-stream packaging.
- Query WS: Sends {type:start|chunk|sources|done}; sources include document_id, filename, chunk_index, content, similarity_score.
- Documents: Background processing generates embeddings and indexes chunks; preserved original uploads.

Frontend (Next.js)
- CenterChat: Added WebSocket streaming; parses and strips JSON matches block from visible answer; falls back to source-based mapping if JSON missing; displays citations.
- RightSidebar: Shows latest results with accurate title, company, match %, skills; added Clear button; "View Full Details" opens the actual PDF via /files or shows a helpful hint if unavailable.

Developer Experience
- Consolidated startup: Replaced setup.ps1, start-backend.ps1, start-frontend.ps1 with a single start.ps1.
- start.ps1 supports tasks: install | backend | frontend | all. It creates venv, installs backend deps, ensures Ollama, installs frontend deps, and launches both services in separate windows.

Usage
- Initial install + run both:
  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\start.ps1 -Task all
- Only install deps:
  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\start.ps1 -Task install
- Only backend:
  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\start.ps1 -Task backend
- Only frontend:
  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\start.ps1 -Task frontend

Notes
- Ollama: If not reachable, the script attempts to start it (ollama serve). If that fails, start manually.
- Models: Ensure your chosen LLM (e.g., llama3.2:latest) and embedding model (e.g., mxbai-embed-large:latest) are installed in Ollama.
- PDFs: Uploaded files are preserved under ./uploads and served at /files for deep links from the UI.
- JSON in chat: The assistant appends a JSON summary of matches to improve the sidebar; the chat UI strips it from display.
